WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.901 --> 00:00:02.100
-You are the coolest.

00:00:02.100 --> 00:00:03.467
I have so many things
to talk to you about.

00:00:03.467 --> 00:00:04.534
Congrats on -- First of all,
Congrats on "This Is Why."

00:00:04.534 --> 00:00:05.634
-Thank you.

00:00:05.634 --> 00:00:06.934
-First album in --
Was it six years?

00:00:06.934 --> 00:00:08.200
-Six years. Yeah.

00:00:08.200 --> 00:00:09.534
-Yeah, and you came on our show,

00:00:09.534 --> 00:00:11.400
and I appreciate that you guys
came on and performed.

00:00:11.400 --> 00:00:12.901
We love you guys.
-That was so fun.

00:00:12.901 --> 00:00:15.567
And now you're doing
"Re: This Is Why,"

00:00:15.567 --> 00:00:16.567
which is "Remix."

00:00:16.567 --> 00:00:18.901
Remix!
-Remix!

00:00:18.901 --> 00:00:21.334
-Why did you end up doing this?

00:00:21.334 --> 00:00:24.400
-So, it's not
a typical remix album.

00:00:24.400 --> 00:00:28.167
We wanted to do something
where we could sort of connect

00:00:28.167 --> 00:00:31.701
with bands that have inspired us
or bands that we've toured

00:00:31.701 --> 00:00:32.968
with that
we really connected with

00:00:32.968 --> 00:00:35.767
and give them a chance
to reinterpret the album.

00:00:35.767 --> 00:00:37.367
-Yeah. I saw
The Linda Lindas on here.

00:00:37.367 --> 00:00:38.834
-Yeah.
-Wet Leg.

00:00:38.834 --> 00:00:41.968
-Mm-hmm. Romy from The xx.
Remi Wolf.

00:00:41.968 --> 00:00:43.701
-Yeah.
-Bartees Strange.

00:00:43.701 --> 00:00:45.334
-Panda Bear. Zane Lowe.

00:00:45.334 --> 00:00:46.934
I mean, this is --
I mean, it's all fun.

00:00:46.934 --> 00:00:48.767
-Yeah, it was such a fun --

00:00:48.767 --> 00:00:50.634
It's very hard
to organize musicians.

00:00:50.634 --> 00:00:51.934
-Yes.

00:00:51.934 --> 00:00:54.667
-Like, we're not the easiest
people to -- You know?

00:00:54.667 --> 00:00:56.000
-No, I do understand. Yeah.

00:00:56.000 --> 00:00:58.767
-So this is a feat.
This is a miracle.

00:00:58.767 --> 00:01:01.133
-You also brought us
some swag from your tour,

00:01:01.133 --> 00:01:02.334
which I was excited about.

00:01:02.334 --> 00:01:04.467
But can you explain
what I'm looking at?

00:01:04.467 --> 00:01:08.267
-Oh, yeah. This shirt
was really popular on the tour.

00:01:08.267 --> 00:01:11.601
So, these are my X-rays
from the chiropractor.

00:01:11.601 --> 00:01:14.200
[ Laughter ]

00:01:14.200 --> 00:01:18.567
I -- For the first 10 years of
our career, we would --

00:01:18.567 --> 00:01:19.834
You know, we were always
the youngest band out,

00:01:19.834 --> 00:01:21.868
and the older dudes
would be like,

00:01:21.868 --> 00:01:23.868
"Oh, you're going to regret
headbanging like that."

00:01:23.868 --> 00:01:26.067
And we were like,
"Nah, you're just really old."

00:01:26.067 --> 00:01:27.167
And --

00:01:27.167 --> 00:01:29.334
-Yeah, you're like,
"What up, old man?

00:01:29.334 --> 00:01:30.567
Just get out of here."

00:01:30.567 --> 00:01:33.601
-Yeah. And so, obviously,
I continued to headbang

00:01:33.601 --> 00:01:35.934
and give myself whiplash
for a really long time.

00:01:35.934 --> 00:01:37.934
And during the break
that we took,

00:01:37.934 --> 00:01:39.601
which was -- We needed it so bad

00:01:39.601 --> 00:01:40.934
and we really wanted
to take a break

00:01:40.934 --> 00:01:43.767
just to kind of be home
and be kind of normal.

00:01:43.767 --> 00:01:44.901
But I woke up one morning.

00:01:44.901 --> 00:01:46.601
I, like,
couldn't look to my left

00:01:46.601 --> 00:01:49.601
and I thought,
"It's time to pay the piper."

00:01:49.601 --> 00:01:52.567
-Yeah. And, so, did you -- Was
something wrong with your neck?

00:01:52.567 --> 00:01:53.834
-Yeah.

00:01:53.834 --> 00:01:57.100
I know a lot about neck bones
at this point.

00:01:57.100 --> 00:02:04.934
My cervical vertebrae,
C-5 and -6, were, like, eroding.

00:02:04.934 --> 00:02:07.033
And I had what's called
military neck.

00:02:07.033 --> 00:02:11.334
Like, I had, like, headbanged
the curvature out of my neck.

00:02:11.334 --> 00:02:14.968
So it just became, like,
a huge part of my life.

00:02:14.968 --> 00:02:16.534
-Does it come back?

00:02:16.534 --> 00:02:19.234
-Well, I'm in, like,
serious P.T. all the time.

00:02:19.234 --> 00:02:21.701
Like, on tour, I'm, like --
I'm trying to get swole

00:02:21.701 --> 00:02:24.801
so that my neck can handle
the headbangs.

00:02:24.801 --> 00:02:27.000
-You're going to continue
to headbang?

00:02:27.000 --> 00:02:29.434
-I have to, Jimmy. It's --
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:29.434 --> 00:02:31.701
-Absolutely not.

00:02:31.701 --> 00:02:37.033
As your father, I'm telling you,
no more headbanging!

00:02:37.033 --> 00:02:40.634
♪♪
No, don't you even start.

00:02:40.634 --> 00:02:43.667
No rock music here.

00:02:43.667 --> 00:02:46.434
How long have you guys
been together, you and the band?

00:02:46.434 --> 00:02:47.501
-We --
-There's you guys.

00:02:47.501 --> 00:02:48.634
-Aww, there we are.

00:02:48.634 --> 00:02:51.300
-Taylor and Zac?
-Yeah. There we are.

00:02:51.300 --> 00:02:54.267
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:54.267 --> 00:02:57.534
Yeah. Oh! Oh, wow, yeah.

00:02:57.534 --> 00:02:59.100
-Who are these --
-That's --

00:02:59.100 --> 00:03:00.501
-Who are these kids?

00:03:00.501 --> 00:03:03.434
-So, this is when we met,
basically,

00:03:03.434 --> 00:03:06.167
This was either 2002 or 2003.

00:03:06.167 --> 00:03:07.267
We've been friends
a long time, man.

00:03:07.267 --> 00:03:08.467
-Yeah, that's a long time.

00:03:08.467 --> 00:03:12.734
-And you can see
our personalities vividly here.

00:03:12.734 --> 00:03:16.400
Taylor stuck to the wall,
glued to the wall,

00:03:16.400 --> 00:03:19.067
in the shadows, me posing,

00:03:19.067 --> 00:03:22.767
Zac being a ham with
a farmer's tan, you can see.

00:03:22.767 --> 00:03:23.834
-Yeah, he's got
a nice farmer's tan.

00:03:23.834 --> 00:03:25.367
-This was Zac's favorite shirt.

00:03:25.367 --> 00:03:26.467
He wore this for every --

00:03:26.467 --> 00:03:27.801
I think he even wore it
in a music video.

00:03:27.801 --> 00:03:31.534
But, yeah,
I was probably 14 here.

00:03:31.534 --> 00:03:33.367
-And who are you listening to?
Who were your influences?

00:03:33.367 --> 00:03:37.501
-Oh, at the time, we were
listening to Deftones a ton,

00:03:37.501 --> 00:03:40.100
like, a lot of heavy music,
but -- And, like, Failure.

00:03:40.100 --> 00:03:42.267
We loved failure.

00:03:42.267 --> 00:03:45.534
But also -- Like,
I mean, I liked The Cure.

00:03:45.534 --> 00:03:49.033
Like, I feel like we got
a pretty good music education.

00:03:49.033 --> 00:03:51.100
But it's kind of funny.

00:03:51.100 --> 00:03:54.467
Like, the first year
that we met,

00:03:54.467 --> 00:03:57.100
there was a really huge hit
that kind of took over

00:03:57.100 --> 00:04:00.968
our little homeschool
tutorial thing.

00:04:00.968 --> 00:04:03.767
-And who was this?
-Do you know?

00:04:03.767 --> 00:04:07.868
It's called "Idiot Boyfriend."
Do you know that song?

00:04:07.868 --> 00:04:10.067
-My song?
-Yeah.

00:04:10.067 --> 00:04:11.267
-My comedy song?
-Yeah.

00:04:11.267 --> 00:04:12.701
-"Idiot Boyfriend"?

00:04:12.701 --> 00:04:16.000
-Huge hit with the
Paramore crew.

00:04:16.000 --> 00:04:17.501
-I was the influence
for Paramore?

00:04:17.501 --> 00:04:19.200
-Yes!

00:04:19.200 --> 00:04:20.968
100%.
-100%?

00:04:20.968 --> 00:04:24.067
-Yeah.
-My disc?

00:04:24.067 --> 00:04:25.434
Really? "Idiot Boyfriend"?

00:04:25.434 --> 00:04:27.868
-1,000%.
The music video -- iconic.

00:04:27.868 --> 00:04:29.300
-That was Zooey Desch--
That was --

00:04:29.300 --> 00:04:30.667
-Yes!

00:04:30.667 --> 00:04:35.133
-I had a disco comedy song
when disco was at its peak.

00:04:35.133 --> 00:04:36.767
2000, 2003.

00:04:36.767 --> 00:04:40.601
-Yes. It was so good.

00:04:40.601 --> 00:04:42.634
-No, it was not.
-Your falsetto.

00:04:42.634 --> 00:04:46.367
-No. Where did you
even hear that song?

00:04:46.367 --> 00:04:48.033
MTV.
-MTV, yes.

00:04:48.033 --> 00:04:50.534
-They're only people
that would -- Thank you, MTV.

00:04:50.534 --> 00:04:53.000
They're the only people that
ever played it ever once.

00:04:53.000 --> 00:04:54.634
-Every morning,
getting ready for, like,

00:04:54.634 --> 00:04:55.901
our homeschool thing --

00:04:55.901 --> 00:04:57.334
It wasn't even, like,
really a school,

00:04:57.334 --> 00:05:00.234
but it was --
We met up to do something

00:05:00.234 --> 00:05:03.601
and, every morning, had MTV on.

00:05:03.601 --> 00:05:06.567
And, like, your song
played more than, like --

00:05:06.567 --> 00:05:09.968
I think John Mayer had a song
out of this at the same time.

00:05:09.968 --> 00:05:11.734
-Yeah. Yeah, we have
similar careers, yeah.

00:05:11.734 --> 00:05:13.334
-You got some spins, man.

00:05:13.334 --> 00:05:15.334
-I got some spins in there.
-Yes.

00:05:15.334 --> 00:05:17.334
-But look at you now.
Look at what I created.

00:05:17.334 --> 00:05:21.968
Oh, my God. I am so happy.
"Re: This Is Why."

00:05:21.968 --> 00:05:23.334
-Yeah.

00:05:23.334 --> 00:05:27.000
-And then, next summer,
you're going to be opening up

00:05:27.000 --> 00:05:29.234
for Taylor Swift
on her Eras Tour.

00:05:29.234 --> 00:05:30.300
[ Cheers and applause ]
-Yes.

00:05:30.300 --> 00:05:31.934
-That's a big deal.
-Yeah.

00:05:31.934 --> 00:05:33.901
But you've known each other
for a while, you and Tay--

00:05:33.901 --> 00:05:35.200
-A long time.

00:05:35.200 --> 00:05:38.100
Yeah, we kind of both
got started around the same time

00:05:38.100 --> 00:05:39.300
and the same age, as well.

00:05:39.300 --> 00:05:40.968
But, like, especially Nashville,

00:05:40.968 --> 00:05:43.033
Nashville's very, like,
family, you know --

00:05:43.033 --> 00:05:44.601
-I love Nashville.
-It's great.

00:05:44.601 --> 00:05:46.300
I really like
our music community.

00:05:46.300 --> 00:05:47.767
Everyone wants to help
each other out.

00:05:47.767 --> 00:05:51.634
And, so, me and Taylor
met because both of us,

00:05:51.634 --> 00:05:54.167
Paramore and Taylor, were
nominated for Best New Artist

00:05:54.167 --> 00:05:55.667
the same year at the Grammys.

00:05:55.667 --> 00:05:58.133
And, so, we were
at some Grammy party.

00:05:58.133 --> 00:06:00.334
It was actually
Timbaland's Grammy party.

00:06:00.334 --> 00:06:04.200
-Wow!
-Huge. I was very nervous.

00:06:04.200 --> 00:06:07.434
But a woman came up to me
and she said,

00:06:07.434 --> 00:06:08.934
"I'm Taylor Swift's mom.

00:06:08.934 --> 00:06:11.167
And, you know,
Taylor doesn't have a lot of

00:06:11.167 --> 00:06:12.601
friends her age that do music.

00:06:12.601 --> 00:06:14.033
And I would love to,
like, you know,

00:06:14.033 --> 00:06:15.767
introduce you guys
or get your number."

00:06:15.767 --> 00:06:18.434
So Andrea, the legend
that she is, like --

00:06:18.434 --> 00:06:19.601
-I love Taylor's mom.
-Yeah, me too.

00:06:19.601 --> 00:06:20.767
-I love Taylor's mom.

00:06:20.767 --> 00:06:23.234
-Yeah, she connected us and --
Yeah.

00:06:23.234 --> 00:06:26.367
-Look, here you guys are.
-There we are.

00:06:26.367 --> 00:06:29.934
Also, every photo of us
that's on the Internet,

00:06:29.934 --> 00:06:32.667
one or both of us is like...

00:06:32.667 --> 00:06:35.000
Like, I don't know why.

00:06:35.000 --> 00:06:36.167
-That's your thing.
-It is our thing.

00:06:36.167 --> 00:06:38.300
-That's your thing.
One of you -- Yeah.

00:06:38.300 --> 00:06:40.400
-It's just to show
how cool we are.

00:06:40.400 --> 00:06:41.567
It's like...

00:06:41.567 --> 00:06:42.734
-Yeah, you don't
have to even do that anymore.

00:06:42.734 --> 00:06:45.567
You're like, "Please."
We have the X-rays.

00:06:45.567 --> 00:06:47.067
You're cool, alright?

00:06:48.868 --> 00:06:51.501
Well, I'm so happy you're here.
Congrats on the album.

00:06:51.501 --> 00:06:54.133
And I want you to be on our show
every album release.

00:06:54.133 --> 00:06:55.901
-Oh, my God, please.
-Yeah.

00:06:55.901 --> 00:06:58.501
And I was thinking about this,
because I saw the pre-interview,

00:06:58.501 --> 00:07:00.367
and I was thinking,
if you wanted to,

00:07:00.367 --> 00:07:02.067
maybe we can go out
to commercial

00:07:02.067 --> 00:07:04.801
doing one of your
earliest influences,

00:07:04.801 --> 00:07:08.534
if you wouldn't mind
singing with me.

00:07:08.534 --> 00:07:10.501
-I would be honored.
♪♪

00:07:15.767 --> 00:07:19.300
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:07:19.300 --> 00:07:21.267
-♪ I know what you want ♪

00:07:23.534 --> 00:07:25.501
♪ And I know what you need ♪

00:07:28.334 --> 00:07:30.400
♪ But I'm gon' screw it up ♪

00:07:30.400 --> 00:07:31.400
♪ Yeah ♪

00:07:31.400 --> 00:07:33.234
♪ Because I'm an idiot ♪

00:07:33.234 --> 00:07:35.033
♪ And I'm your boyfriend ♪

00:07:35.033 --> 00:07:37.434
♪ Yes, I am ♪

00:07:37.434 --> 00:07:39.667
-♪ And I'm gonna take you out ♪

00:07:42.167 --> 00:07:44.767
♪ Leave my wallet home ♪

00:07:46.801 --> 00:07:50.067
♪ Then I'll use
your cellphone, baby ♪

00:07:50.067 --> 00:07:51.767
♪ Long distance ♪

00:07:51.767 --> 00:07:54.300
♪ 'Cause I'm your boyfriend ♪

00:07:54.300 --> 00:07:56.934
-Hayley Williams, everybody!
Come on!

00:07:56.934 --> 00:07:59.033
That's what I'm talking about.

00:07:59.033 --> 00:08:01.467
We'll be right back
with Maluma, everybody.

00:08:01.467 --> 00:08:03.167
Come on back.

00:08:03.167 --> 00:08:05.133
Oh!

00:08:05.133 --> 00:08:07.901
♪ And I know what you need ♪

00:08:10.000 --> 00:08:13.033
♪ Leave my wallet at home ♪

00:08:13.033 --> 00:08:14.467
I can't believe you know this.
-[ Laughs ]

